  "details": "Hi. Yes. I still have barely any usability for vrchat since the removal of mod support. It's nearly been a year since the addition of EAC.\n\nI have severe night blindness rendering worlds that are too dark barely visible for me, I essentially relied on injecting shaders and color grading to work around this. \n\nI shouldn't need to rely on world creators being psychic and making every world compliant to my disability. I should expect vrchat to just have a brightness slider\n\nAnother side effect of this is sensativity to oversaturated light sources basically being very blinding on occasion, if something in a world has glow/bloom cranked up way too high, and i cannot disable it, it induces headaches and severe eye strain.\n\nAll I ask is for the ability to disable post-procressing at a client side level in worlds that are too dark, or even a basic brightness slider",
